        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): reload edited hook transforms",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where editing a configured hook transform could leave the gateway running the old transform function after hooks hot reload rebuilt the mapping config.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nHook mapping resolution now builds a candidate runtime snapshot without mutating the process-local transform cache. The transform cache generation is advanced only after the gateway accepts the new hooks runtime config at startup or at the hot-reload commit edge. A delayed import from an older generation can still finish its own delivery, but it no longer republishes into the current cache after an accepted reload, and a rejected candidate reload leaves the active transform cache untouched.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can update hook transform files and have subsequent matching webhook deliveries use the edited transform without restarting the gateway.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Production module boundary: `pnpm exec tsx ../../outputs/local-hook-transform-reload/proof-live.ts`\n\n```text\n$ pnpm exec tsx ../../outputs/local-hook-transform-reload/proof-live.ts\nfirst-transform: before\nafter-rejected-candidate: before\nafter-reload: after\n```\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/hooks-mapping.test.ts`: 31 passed, including rejected-candidate and overlapping-import regressions.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/config-reload.test.ts`: 132 passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-reload-handlers.test.ts`: 97 passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-runtime-config.test.ts`: 30 passed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\n<details>\n<summary>proof-live.ts</summary>\n\n```ts\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { pathToFileURL } from \"node:url\";\n\nconst configDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"openclaw-hook-transform-proof-\"));\nconst transformsRoot = path.join(configDir, \"hooks\", \"transforms\");\nfs.mkdirSync(transformsRoot, { recursive: true });\nconst transformPath = path.join(transformsRoot, \"reloadable.mjs\");\n\ntype HooksMappingModule = typeof import(\"./src/gateway/hooks-mapping.js\");\nlet hooksMapping: HooksMappingModule;\n\nfunction writeTransform(text: string) {\n  fs.writeFileSync(\n    transformPath,\n    `export default () => ({ kind: \"wake\", text: ${JSON.stringify(text)} });\\n`,\n  );\n}\n\nfunction resolveCurrentMappings() {\n  return hooksMapping.resolveHookMappings(\n    {\n      mappings: [\n        {\n          match: { path: \"reloadable\" },\n          action: \"agent\",\n          messageTemplate: \"unused\",\n          transform: { module: \"reloadable.mjs\" },\n        },\n      ],\n    },\n    { configDir },\n  );\n}\n\nfunction acceptMappings(mappings: ReturnType<typeof resolveCurrentMappings>) {\n  hooksMapping.commitHookTransformMappingReload();\n  return mappings;\n}\n\nasync function runHook(mappings: ReturnType<typeof resolveCurrentMappings>) {\n  const result = await hooksMapping.applyHookMappings(mappings, {\n    payload: {},\n    headers: {},\n    url: new URL(\"http://127.0.0.1:18789/hooks/reloadable\"),\n    path: \"reloadable\",\n  });\n  if (!result?.ok || result.action?.kind !== \"wake\") {\n    throw new Error(`unexpected hook result: ${JSON.stringify(result)}`);\n  }\n  return result.action.text;\n}\n\nasync function main() {\n  hooksMapping = await import(pathToFileURL(path.resolve(\"src/gateway/hooks-mapping.ts\")).href);\n  try {\n    writeTransform(\"before\");\n    let mappings = acceptMappings(resolveCurrentMappings());\n    console.log(`first-transform: ${await runHook(mappings)}`);\n    writeTransform(\"after\");\n    resolveCurrentMappings(); // rejected candidate resolution must not invalidate the active cache\n    console.log(`after-rejected-candidate: ${await runHook(mappings)}`);\n    mappings = acceptMappings(resolveCurrentMappings());\n    console.log(`after-reload: ${await runHook(mappings)}`);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(configDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n}\n\nvoid main();\n```\n\n</details>\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
